{
  "id": "gittensor-model-hub_sparkdistill_232",
  "repo_name": "gittensor-model-hub/sparkdistill",
  "repo_url": "https://github.com/gittensor-model-hub/sparkdistill",
  "base_commit": "94d5c864a5c8e5b8baae1f9238146eaa2fe1c574",
  "pr_number": 232,
  "issue_number": 231,
  "issue_title": "Canonical-pin grace window is dropped in eval.verify, so honest training PRs are auto-closed as eval:REJECT",
  "issue_body": "**Summary.** The canonical-pin grace window added by [#121](https://github.com/gittensor-model-hub/SparkDistill/pull/121) (for issue #118) is applied in only two of the three places that check `mix_manifest.sft_sha256`. The third \u2014 `eval.verify.verify_submission`, reached through `verify_remote_proof_bundle_scores` \u2014 still compares against **live HEAD only**. An honest training-track PR whose pin advanced mid-training therefore passes stage 1 and is then rejected in stage 2 with `eval:REJECT`, which `training_track.yml` runs with `--close-on-reject` \u2192 **the PR is auto-closed**. Issue #118 reproduces through a different code path.\n\n**Where the window is honoured**\n- `validate_pr_body_canonical_pin(pr_body, acceptable_sft_shas=...)` \u2705\n- `verify_remote_proof_bundle(repo_id, acceptable_sft_shas=...)` \u2705\n\n**Where it is dropped** \u2014 `eval/training_track_gate.py`:\n\n```python\n# gate_training_pr(): the window is computed...\nacceptable_sft_shas = _canonical_sft_sha256s_for_pr_window(\n    merge_base_ref=merge_base_ref, head_ref=\"HEAD\"\n)\n...\n# ...but verify_remote_proof_bundle_scores() never receives it, so\n# _download_and_verify_bundle() calls:\nreport = verify_submission(bundle_dir, frontier, attestation=attestation)\n```\n\n`verify_submission()` has no `acceptable_sft_shas` parameter at all, so `check_canonical_dataset_claim(manifest, bundle_dir=bundle_dir)` falls back to `allowed = {canonical_sft_sha256()}` \u2014 the single pin at the checked-out tree, which `training_track.yml` checks out from `pull_request.base.ref` (live `main`).\n\n**Reproduction** (bundle pinned to the merge-base sha, window = {base, head}):\n\n```\nstage 1  verify_remote_proof_bundle  -> []                         # accepted\nstage 2  verify_remote_proof_bundle_scores\n         issues: ['eval.verify canonical_dataset_failed: bundle mix_manifest.sft_sha256\n                   does not match an accepted canonical pin (allowed 1 pin(s) for this PR window)']\n         eval_label: eval:REJECT\n```\n\nThe message itself reports `allowed 1 pin(s)` \u2014 the grace set never arrived.\n\n**Impact**\n1. **Honest training PRs are auto-closed.** `main()` closes on `training:REJECT`, and `eval:REJECT` is in `_AUTO_CLOSE_EVAL_LABELS`. This is exactly the \"miners burn GPU with no reachable success state\" failure #118 documents, and it silently contradicts the PR template, which promises *\"any pin from merge-base through HEAD is accepted\"*.\n2. **Closed PRs damage miner credibility.** Under SN74 scoring, `credibility = merged/(merged+closed)` gates eligibility at 80% and multiplies earned score \u2014 an automated wrong-close costs the miner far more than the single submission.\n3. **The merged ledger is corrupted too.** `record_merged_ledger_entry` shares `_download_and_verify_bundle`, so an already-merged run can be recorded `eval:REJECT` and its `runs/frontiers.json` update skipped \u2014 the pin can advance again between the gate job and the ledger job. A missing frontier raise then mis-tiers every later submission.\n\n**Suggested fix.** Thread the window already computed in `gate_training_pr` down through `verify_remote_proof_bundle_scores` \u2192 `_download_and_verify_bundle` \u2192 `verify_submission` \u2192 `check_canonical_dataset_claim` (which already accepts `acceptable_sft_shas`), and give `record_merged_ledger_entry` the PR's `merge_base_ref` so the merge-time path computes the same window. Defaulting the new parameter to `None` keeps the standalone `python -m eval.verify` validator path strict (HEAD pin only) and is fully backward compatible.\n\nHappy to open the PR \u2014 I have the fix and regression tests ready.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-25T04:22:05.000Z",
